/T (The 2026 FIFA World Cup in the United States, Canada and Mexico is the 23rd edition of the World Cup since the first one in 1930 and the first 48 team tournament. The FIFA World Cup had used the 32 team format for 24 years up until 2026 when it was changed to 48. The expansion was meant to increase global representation and introduce new nations to the tournament, with FIFA executives praising the format for giving more countries the opportunity to compete on football's biggest stage. When the expansion was first announced, it arrived with a lot of backlash, mainly from European teams and UEFA president Aleksander Ceferin, with complaints about the quality of the tournament reducing. )
/E (The 2026 FIFA World Cup in the United States, Canada and Mexico is the 23rd edition of the World Cup since the first one in 1930 and the first 48 team tournament. The FIFA World Cup had used the 32 team format for 24 years up until 2026 when it was changed to 48. The expansion was meant to increase global representation and introduce new nations to the tournament, with FIFA executives praising the format for giving more countries the opportunity to compete on football's biggest stage. When the expansion was first announced, it arrived with a lot of backlash, mainly from European teams and UEFA president Aleksander Ceferin, with complaints about the quality of the tournament reducing. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
