/P 166 0 R
/T (In 2025 CONMEBOL brought a proposal to increase the number of participating teams in the World Cup to 64 from 2030 which was initially ignored by most of the footballing world; that all changed after the relative success of the 2026 World Cup where most of the pre tournament concerns were disproved. A further expansion of the World Cup would immensely benefit smaller nations aspiring to qualify for the tournament, the money they would receive from just qualifying for one World Cup could change the football landscape of those nations,the type of money they could reinvest into stadiums, youth facilities and scouting programs. One of the main criticisms of the 48-team tournament was the reintroduction of third-place group finishers potentially moving on to the knockout phase.)
/E (In 2025 CONMEBOL brought a proposal to increase the number of participating teams in the World Cup to 64 from 2030 which was initially ignored by most of the footballing world; that all changed after the relative success of the 2026 World Cup where most of the pre tournament concerns were disproved. A further expansion of the World Cup would immensely benefit smaller nations aspiring to qualify for the tournament, the money they would receive from just qualifying for one World Cup could change the football landscape of those nations,the type of money they could reinvest into stadiums, youth facilities and scouting programs. One of the main criticisms of the 48-team tournament was the reintroduction of third-place group finishers potentially moving on to the knockout phase.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
304 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 166 0 R
/T (The odd math of the top eight third-place finishers from 12 groups moving on led to some confusing scenarios in the final days of group play, not to mention some teams waiting several days to learn their round of 32 opponents. But then for the bigger nations and star players, a 64 team World Cup would mean a more congested club season in an already tightly packed club season where players are at the greatest injury risk ever due to the high intensity of games played and the sheer volume of the games in a season, with the best club players playing close to 60 games a season and some playing 3 games a week. In its initial 16-team format, the World Cup was hosted by smaller nations like Uruguay, Hungary and Sweden.)
/E (The odd math of the top eight third-place finishers from 12 groups moving on led to some confusing scenarios in the final days of group play, not to mention some teams waiting several days to learn their round of 32 opponents. But then for the bigger nations and star players, a 64 team World Cup would mean a more congested club season in an already tightly packed club season where players are at the greatest injury risk ever due to the high intensity of games played and the sheer volume of the games in a season, with the best club players playing close to 60 games a season and some playing 3 games a week. In its initial 16-team format, the World Cup was hosted by smaller nations like Uruguay, Hungary and Sweden.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
305 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 166 0 R
/T (Those days have already long departed. But the 128-match calendar of a 64-team field -- necessitating the use of at least 20-22 stadiums -- would mean only a few nations could truly host the event themselves. And if co-hosting becomes the norm, that would be a considerable departure from the past. The 2026 tournament was only the second to be hosted by two or more nations \(following Korea-Japan in 2002\).)
/E (Those days have already long departed. But the 128-match calendar of a 64-team field -- necessitating the use of at least 20-22 stadiums -- would mean only a few nations could truly host the event themselves. And if co-hosting becomes the norm, that would be a considerable departure from the past. The 2026 tournament was only the second to be hosted by two or more nations \(following Korea-Japan in 2002\).)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
