<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 170 0 R
/E (Focuses on the physical and mental strain imposed on athletes by an expanded match calendar. Extending the World Cup to accommodate 128 matches over roughly six weeks forces players to navigate extra knockout rounds alongside an already bloated domestic and international club schedule. Drastically reduced off-season recovery time significantly increases the risk of fatigue, burnout, and career-threatening injuries among elite players, ultimately undermining the quality of play across both club and international football.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
