346 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 170 0 R
/E (Highlights the tension between FIFA's commercial incentives and the financial realities faced by host nations. For governing bodies and broadcasters, a 64-team spectacle offers unprecedented revenue opportunities through expanded media rights, global corporate sponsorships, and ticket sales. However, host countries must absorb colossal expenditures to construct or upgrade world-class stadiums, training facilities, and public transit networks, raising serious questions about whether long-term economic returns justify such massive public investment.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
