/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 171 0 R
/E (Addresses the daunting operational demands required to host a 128-match tournament. The sheer footprint of a 64-team event makes multi-country hosting bids virtually mandatory, requiring seamless cross-border coordination, unified security protocols, and vast transport networks. Additionally, the constant long-distance travel required for 64 national squads and millions of traveling supporters across multiple host nations generates a massive carbon footprint, presenting major environmental and logistical challenges for organizing committees.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
360 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 171 0 R
/E (Weighs the benefits of broader international inclusion against the day-to-day realities for traveling supporters. Expanding qualification spots democratizes global football by granting smaller or historically overlooked nations a platform on the sport's grandest stage, driving grassroots growth worldwide. Conversely, the skyrocketing costs of attending a longer, multi-national tournament risk pricing out traditional match-going supporters in favor of corporate hospitality, threatening the authentic fan culture that makes the World Cup unique.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
