/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 173 0 R
/E (Beyond traditional sportsbooks, FIFA has simultaneously expanded its broader betting infrastructure by centralizing live, real-time match data distribution and establishing commercial partnerships with prediction market platforms. While this commercial strategy has unlocked record sponsorship revenues across expanded 48-team, 104-match tournament formats, it has also sparked controversy. Integrity organizations, such as the Council of Europe, have expressed concern over the rapid growth of micro-moment in-play markets, pointing out that wagering on isolated match actions increases vulnerabilities to spot-fixing. Despite these ongoing regulatory debates, sports wagering and event-trading platforms remain anchored as permanent commercial pillars within international football governance.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
