/P 174 0 R
/E (A major change occurred on May 14, 2018, when the U.S. Supreme Court struck down the Professional and Amateur Sports Protection Act \(PASPA\) in Murphy v. NCAA. The decision allowed individual U.S. states to legalize and regulate sports betting. This transformed the economic environment surrounding sports wagering, encouraging major sports organizations to consider betting as a legitimate commercial opportunity rather than solely an integrity threat. The growing North American market became particularly significant ahead of the 2026 FIFA World Cup.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
