/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 176 0 R
/E (Unlike traditional match-outcome betting \(e.g., picking the winner\), modern sportsbooks emphasize in-play micro-betting. Fans can wager on hyper-specific moments: who takes the next throw-in, whether a player receives a yellow card, or how many corner kicks occur in a five-minute window.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
437 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 176 0 R
/E (Integrity officials point out that micro-betting dramatically increases vulnerability to spot-fixing. It requires only a single rogue player or official to trigger a payout without changing the final score. Regulators warn that expanding these markets during massive events like the 48-team World Cup creates significant enforcement challenges across global jurisdictions.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
