1729 0 obj
<<
/Title (The 2026 FIFA World Cup in the United States, Canada and Mexico is the 23rd edition of the World Cup since the first one in 1930 and the first 48 team tournament. The FIFA World Cup had used the 32 team format for 24 years up until 2026 when it was changed to 48. The expansion was meant to increase global representation and introduce new nations to the tournament, with FIFA executives praising the format for giving more countries the opportunity to compete on football's biggest stage. When the expansion was first announced, it arrived with a lot of backlash, mainly from European teams and UEFA president Aleksander Ceferin, with complaints about the quality of the tournament reducing.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1702 0 R
/Prev 1719 0 R
/Next 1720 0 R
>>
endobj
1730 0 obj
<<
/Title (In 2025 CONMEBOL brought a proposal to increase the number of participating teams in the World Cup to 64 from 2030 which was initially ignored by most of the footballing world; that all changed after the relative success of the 2026 World Cup where most of the pre tournament concerns were disproved. A further expansion of the World Cup would immensely benefit smaller nations aspiring to qualify for the tournament, the money they would receive from just qualifying for one World Cup could change the football landscape of those nations,the type of money they could reinvest into stadiums, youth facilities and scouting programs. One of the main criticisms of the 48-team tournament was the reintroduction of third-place group finishers potentially moving on to the knockout phase.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1721 0 R
/Next 1741 0 R
>>
endobj
1731 0 obj
<<
/Title (Finally, the constant changing of the football calendar and qualifying campaigns is making football more and more volatile, a major problem we as a committee are striving to solve.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1721 0 R
/Prev 1742 0 R
>>
endobj
