<<
/Title (The odd math of the top eight third-place finishers from 12 groups moving on led to some confusing scenarios in the final days of group play, not to mention some teams waiting several days to learn their round of 32 opponents. But then for the bigger nations and star players, a 64 team World Cup would mean a more congested club season in an already tightly packed club season where players are at the greatest injury risk ever due to the high intensity of games played and the sheer volume of the games in a season, with the best club players playing close to 60 games a season and some playing 3 games a week. In its initial 16-team format, the World Cup was hosted by smaller nations like Uruguay, Hungary and Sweden.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1721 0 R
/Prev 1730 0 R
/Next 1742 0 R
>>
endobj
1742 0 obj
<<
/Title (Those days have already long departed. But the 128-match calendar of a 64-team field -- necessitating the use of at least 20-22 stadiums -- would mean only a few nations could truly host the event themselves. And if co-hosting becomes the norm, that would be a considerable departure from the past. The 2026 tournament was only the second to be hosted by two or more nations \(following Korea-Japan in 2002\).)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1721 0 R
/Prev 1741 0 R
/Next 1731 0 R
>>
endobj
